# Angel Island ACT 1=
# ((A,B),(X,Y))
# Both are big endian 16 bit, but Y is inverted (up=subtract, down=add)

# Step 15: start-zone kill checkpoint - ends a non-progressing episode immediately
# instead of burning the whole step budget wandering near spawn. Real spawn position
# measured directly via env.reset()+first step(): x=5002, y=1051 (confirmed, not
# assumed - see AGENTS.md "Step 15"). This box's x range [5010,5045] deliberately
# excludes x=5002 on the low side (8px margin) and stays below the next box's x_min=5050
# on the high side (5px margin), so it can never trigger on the literal spawn frame.
# Real per-step x deltas measured from an actual demo's first 40 steps near the start:
# max +2px/step, so a 35px-wide box has a large tunneling safety margin at this point in
# the level (nowhere near the fast-moving/camera-locked segments that forced the
# narrow-box threshold redesigns elsewhere in this file). [disable_after: initial
# checkpoint] makes this permanently inert for the rest of the episode the moment the
# very next real checkpoint is reached, so a later legitimate backtrack into this x/y
# region can't retroactively kill an otherwise-successful run.
((5010,0),(5045,1135)) [disable_after: initial checkpoint] # start-zone kill checkpoint, non-progressing episode

