# Step 22: merged in from coords_captured_from_foxo.list - Foxo's own hands-on Debug
# Mode pass through the rest of AIZ1 (the continuation past the cutscene, through to
# the miniboss). Raw file kept as coords_captured_from_foxo.list for reference. This
# whole continuation has NOT been cross-validated against real demo footage the way
# the boxes above were (all 5 real human demos truncate at the original cutscene
# trigger, before any of this) - trusted as real, hands-on-gathered data per the
# same process as every other coords.list addition, just without that specific
# extra layer of verification this project used everywhere else.
#
# Needs CheckpointTracker(boxes, extend_past_end=True) to actually continue past the
# "end"-kind box above instead of terminating there - see checkpoints.py "Step 21".
# Default (extend_past_end=False) behavior for the box above is UNCHANGED, so
# ingest_demo.py/bc_pretrain.py/check_bc_fit_real.py's existing BC-pretraining use of
# it as the demo-truncation point keeps working exactly as before.
#
# Two near-identical "loop" box pairs appear below (e.g. two separate "Loop
# entry"/"Loop top"/"Loop left"/"Loop exit" sets at slightly different coordinates) -
# flagging rather than merging/deleting either: could be two different real routes
# through the same loop traced on different attempts, intentionally kept distinct -
# left exactly as given.
#
# Step 22 fix, caught by the same verification test as the boss-trigger one below:
# this threshold (472) is numerically SMALLER than the OLD space's spawn position
# itself (x=5002) - without a prerequisite it would fire within the first few steps
# of EVERY episode, immediately after spawn, nowhere near any real cutscene.
# [requires: interactive-cutscene trigger] ties it to the real "end"-kind box
# (x>=12210) genuinely having been visited first - the box below (boss trigger) and
# the TODO one both chain off THIS box's prerequisite, so fixing it here closes the
# loophole for the whole chain, not just patching further down.

